  "interpretation_requirements": [
    "Four distinct scenes measured at two SNR values, not eight independent scenes. This is the reused development cohort, not an independent confirmation.",
    "The -8 dB metric is the first index of a ten-point window in the pooled active-user raw-denoising NMSE. It is offline truth-based scoring, not an online stop and not per-scene hitting time. Confirmation occurs nine iterations after the reported start.",
    "Native-stop medians omit nonconverged runs; always show converged count. All eight new_I weight .4 runs stop at the configured minimum 60, so the rule censors faster convergence.",
    "At weight .4, new_C pooled variance is floored in 336/480 (-4 dB) and 339/480 (0 dB) iterations: 70.0% and 70.625%; the approximate 70% statement is not a claim for every weight. New_I .4 also floors 108/480 and 123/480: 22.5% and 25.625%.",
    "Do not describe weight .6 as failing every run: new_I converges in one -4 dB case, new_C in one case at each SNR, but pooled outcomes are poor and most runs fail. Convergence alone does not establish zero detection error.",
    "Across old/new models, mean model, training epoch, variance interface, and compatibility with the frozen classifier differ. Within-new-model .2-to-.4 results support an empirical damping effect, not a pure neural-architecture cause or universally optimal weight.",
    "Runtime is descriptive under concurrent load. Earlier threshold starts or fewer iterations do not imply faster wall-clock completion. new_I .4 median native-stop times remain above old .2 at both SNR values.",
    "Negative colored probes are not physical negative covariance proof; the noncommuting counterexample and fixed-probe adaptation caveat in REVIEW.json still apply."
  ]
